
-- Batch 1: African recipes (Algeria through Cameroon) - Add continent and history
UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Chakhchoukha is a beloved Algerian dish from the Biskra region in the Saharan highlands. Dating back centuries, it consists of torn flatbread (rougag) layered with a rich tomato-based stew. The dish is central to Berber culinary traditions and is often served during festive occasions and family gatherings. The name comes from the sound of tearing the bread.' WHERE slug = 'chakhchoukha-biskra-algeria';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Trida is a traditional Algerian handmade pasta dish passed down through generations. The pasta is crafted by hand into small squares or rectangles and cooked with chicken in a fragrant broth. This dish showcases the Maghrebi tradition of artisanal pasta-making, influenced by both Berber and Mediterranean culinary heritage.' WHERE slug = 'trida-handmade-pasta-chicken-algeria';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Poulet Moambe (Muamba) is the national dish of both Angola and the DRC, representing Central African culinary excellence. Made with palm butter (moambe), chicken, and spices, it dates back centuries as a ceremonial dish. The rich, earthy palm sauce reflects the palm oil trade that shaped Central African economies and cuisines.' WHERE slug = 'poulet-moambe-muamba-angola-drc';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Calulu de Peixe is a quintessential Angolan and São Toméan fish stew combining dried and fresh fish with vegetables in palm oil. This dish represents the Portuguese colonial influence blended with African ingredients. It was traditionally prepared by fishing communities along the Atlantic coast and remains a staple comfort food.' WHERE slug = 'calulu-de-peixe-angola-sao-tome';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Sauce Gumbo is a beloved okra-based stew originating from the coastal regions of Benin and Togo. The dish showcases the importance of okra in West African cuisine, where it has been cultivated for millennia. The slimy texture of okra, prized for its thickening properties, makes this a hearty accompaniment to starches like fufu.' WHERE slug = 'sauce-gumbo-okra-stew-benin-togo';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Kooso is a traditional Burkinabè dish of steamed millet balls, representing the staple grain culture of the Sahel region. Millet has sustained communities in Burkina Faso for over 4,000 years due to its drought resistance. These nutritious balls are typically served with soups or stews and remain a breakfast staple.' WHERE slug = 'kooso-bf';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Morogo refers to wild spinach or amaranth greens treasured in Botswana and South Africa. These indigenous leafy greens have been foraged and cultivated by San and Bantu peoples for thousands of years. Rich in nutrients, morogo is stewed with onions, tomatoes, and spices, representing African superfood traditions.' WHERE slug = 'morogo-amaranth-greens-botswana-sa';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Achu and Yellow Soup is a ceremonial dish from the Grassfields region of Cameroon, particularly among the Bamileke and Bamenda peoples. The pounded cocoyam (achu) paired with the vibrant yellow palm oil soup is served at important celebrations, weddings, and traditional ceremonies. The dish symbolizes prosperity and community.' WHERE slug = 'achu-yellow-soup-cameroon';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Koki is a traditional Cameroonian black-eyed pea pudding wrapped and steamed in banana leaves. Originating from the Bamileke people of western Cameroon, it represents ancient West African legume preparation techniques. The dish is labor-intensive, involving grinding the peas and carefully steaming them until firm yet moist.' WHERE slug = 'koki-black-eyed-pea-pudding-cameroon';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Cassava fries are a popular street food across the Democratic Republic of Congo, reflecting cassava''s importance as a staple crop introduced from South America in the 16th century. Crispy on the outside and soft inside, these fries represent how Congolese cuisine adapted foreign ingredients into beloved local dishes.' WHERE slug = 'cassava-fries-cd';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Kanda Ti Nyma is a traditional meat and vegetable stew from the Central African Republic. The dish combines local ingredients with techniques passed down through generations. It represents the Central African tradition of communal eating, where families gather around a single pot to share meals.' WHERE slug = 'kanda-ti-nyma-car';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Daraba is a traditional Chadian dish made with okra, meat, and leafy greens in a rich peanut butter sauce. It reflects the culinary traditions of the Sahel region where peanuts and okra are dietary staples. The dish showcases Chad''s position at the crossroads of North and Central African cuisines.' WHERE slug = 'daraba-chad';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Puff Puff is a beloved West African fried dough popular across Cameroon, Nigeria, and Ghana. These sweet, airy balls of fried batter have origins in various African dough traditions and show some similarity to beignets and mandazi. Sold by street vendors and made at home for celebrations, puff puff is essential to West African snack culture.' WHERE slug = 'puff-puff-cm';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Skoudehkaris is Djibouti''s national dish, a fragrant rice and meat preparation reflecting the country''s position on ancient trade routes. The dish shows Arab, Ethiopian, and Somali influences with its use of spices like cardamom and cinnamon. It''s traditionally served on a communal platter for family gatherings.' WHERE slug = 'skoudehkaris-djibouti';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Fumbwa is a traditional Congolese dish made from cassava leaves (saka saka) cooked with palm oil, fish, or meat. The dish represents the DRC''s rich forest ecology and the importance of cassava, which provides both roots and leaves for nutrition. Fumbwa is considered soul food across Central Africa.' WHERE slug = 'fumbwa-drc';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Liboké de Poisson is a traditional Congolese dish where fish is wrapped in banana leaves with vegetables and spices, then steamed or grilled. This cooking method preserves nutrients and infuses the fish with aromatic flavors. The technique dates back centuries and represents sustainable cooking practices in Central Africa.' WHERE slug = 'liboke-de-poisson-drc';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Chapati with Kidney Bean Stew represents the fusion of Indian and East African cuisines. Chapati was introduced to East Africa by Indian railway workers in the late 19th century and became a staple. Paired with local bean stews, this dish symbolizes the multicultural culinary landscape of Kenya, Tanzania, and Uganda.' WHERE slug = 'chapati-with-kidney-bean-stew';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Dukkah is an Egyptian spice and nut blend dating back to ancient times. The word comes from the Arabic "to pound," referring to the traditional preparation method. Egyptians have enjoyed dukkah with bread and olive oil for millennia, and it represents the sophisticated spice culture of North Africa.' WHERE slug = 'dukkah-nuts-eg';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Falafel has ancient roots in Egypt, where it''s called ta''ameya and traditionally made with fava beans rather than chickpeas. Some historians trace its origins to Coptic Christians seeking meat alternatives during Lent. Egyptian falafel remains distinctively green from fresh herbs and is a beloved street food across Cairo.' WHERE slug = 'falafel-balls-eg';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Egyptian falafel with tahini showcases the importance of sesame in Middle Eastern and North African cuisine. The combination of crispy falafel with creamy tahini represents thousands of years of culinary evolution along the Nile. This dish is quintessential Egyptian street food, served in pita with fresh vegetables.' WHERE slug = 'falafel-bites-eg';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Koshari is Egypt''s beloved national dish, a hearty mix of rice, lentils, pasta, and crispy onions topped with spiced tomato sauce. It emerged in the 19th century, possibly influenced by Indian khichri brought by British colonizers. Originally a poor person''s meal, it''s now enjoyed by all social classes across Egypt.' WHERE slug = 'koshari-lentil-sauce-egypt';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Tsebhi Derho is Eritrea''s beloved chicken stew, similar to Ethiopian Doro Wat but with distinct Eritrean spicing. The dish features berbere spice and is traditionally served with injera. It represents the culinary traditions of the Tigrinya people and is central to holiday celebrations and special occasions.' WHERE slug = 'tsebhi-derho-eritrea';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Sidvudvu is a traditional Eswatini (Swaziland) dish made from pumpkin or squash. The dish represents the agricultural heritage of the Swazi people and their traditional reliance on indigenous vegetables. It''s often prepared during cultural celebrations and represents the simple yet nourishing cuisine of Southern Africa.' WHERE slug = 'sidvudvu-eswatini';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Injera is the cornerstone of Ethiopian and Eritrean cuisine, a spongy sourdough flatbread made from teff flour. Archaeological evidence suggests teff cultivation in Ethiopia dates back to 4000-1000 BCE. The unique fermentation process and porous texture make injera both a plate and utensil, embodying communal dining traditions.' WHERE slug = 'injera-et';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'Africa', history = 'Shiro is a beloved Ethiopian chickpea or broad bean flour stew, essential during fasting periods observed by Ethiopian Orthodox Christians. The dish represents the sophisticated vegetarian tradition of Ethiopia, where nearly half the year involves religious fasting. Shiro''s smooth, savory flavor comes from berbere spice and niter kibbeh butter.' WHERE slug = 'shiro-et';
